WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.013
Zann's heart pounded as more nomads stepped into view.

2
00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:18.314
They didn't look friendly.

3
00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:21.517
"Whatever she did, we're sorry," he said.

4
00:00:22.257 --> 00:00:24.018
He assumed they were talking about Wyssa.

5
00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:27.101
"Silence!" an older nomad said.

6
00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:30.463
"What could she have done that was so terrible, anyway?"

7
00:00:30.843 --> 00:00:31.464
Perda cried.

8
00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.994
"Magic barely works here."

9
00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:35.635
Zann nodded.

10
00:00:35.655 --> 00:00:38.237
"And she only arrived an hour ago!"

11
00:00:38.257 --> 00:00:39.959
"An hour?"

12
00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:41.880
The first nomad frowned.

13
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.643
"Telling lies will not help you."

14
00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:46.944
Another nomad stepped forward.

15
00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:50.628
"Your friend has been troubling us for days with his magic."

16
00:00:51.628 --> 00:00:52.449
His magic?

17
00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.331
Zann was confused.

18
00:00:55.191 --> 00:00:56.092
"Wait," he said.

19
00:00:56.112 --> 00:01:00.476
"The only friends we have here are an old woman and a Red girl around our age.

20
00:01:00.952 --> 00:01:02.153
Who are you talking about?"

21
00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:04.275
A nomad woman scowled.

22
00:01:04.295 --> 00:01:07.337
"Don't try to trick us," she snapped.

23
00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:10.360
"Your friend Morb tried that already."

24
00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:12.341
Perda gasped.

25
00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:16.885
"Morb?" "Morb definitely isn't our friend!"

26
00:01:17.266 --> 00:01:17.906
Zann cried.

27
00:01:18.687 --> 00:01:19.447
Darb nodded.

28
00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:21.549
"We came here to stop him."

29
00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.592
The nomads exchanged a skeptical look.

30
00:01:25.532 --> 00:01:28.775
"What would make a bunch of kids think they could stop Morb?"

31
00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:29.776
one asked.

32
00:01:30.508 --> 00:01:33.450
"Because we've done it before," Perda retorted.

33
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.052
"That's right," Zann said.

34
00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:38.714
"We stopped him when he tried to take over Magica.

35
00:01:39.174 --> 00:01:40.855
And when he tried to destroy it after that."

36
00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:44.858
A nomad stepped forward and peered carefully at Zann.

37
00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:49.021
Then she moved over to examine Perda and Darb too.

38
00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.583
Finally she nodded.

39
00:01:52.203 --> 00:01:53.624
"They're right," she said.

40
00:01:53.644 --> 00:01:56.947
"These are three of the young heroes from First City.

41
00:01:57.507 --> 00:01:58.708
I recognize them now!"

42
00:01:59.668 --> 00:02:02.890
"Untie them at once," the older nomad ordered the others.

43
00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.072
Soon Zann and his friends were on their feet.

44
00:02:09.093 --> 00:02:11.835
Now Zann could see the hoof beasts they'd been riding.

45
00:02:12.635 --> 00:02:15.437
They were grazing on some plants a little farther down the trail.

46
00:02:16.237 --> 00:02:19.939
Zann rubbed a spot on his wrist where the rope had bitten into his skin.

47
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:26.043
He was tempted to magically heal it, but he decided that using magic right now probably wasn't a

48
00:02:26.103 --> 00:02:26.643
good idea.

49
00:02:26.663 --> 00:02:33.239
"Please." The older nomad, who appeared to be the leader, gestured toward a cave nearby.

50
00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:35.341
"Come inside and rest."

51
00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:37.903
Another nomad glanced around.

52
00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:42.406
"You shouldn't be out in the open where Morb might spot you," she said.

53
00:02:42.426 --> 00:02:44.767
"He is a dangerous man."

54
00:02:44.787 --> 00:02:47.429
"We know," Perda said.

55
00:02:47.449 --> 00:02:49.931
"That's why we can't rest.

56
00:02:50.371 --> 00:02:51.932
Our friends are still out there!"

57
00:02:52.773 --> 00:02:54.454
A nomad put a hand on her arm.

58
00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:57.296
"Perhaps we can send out a search party.

59
00:02:57.932 --> 00:02:59.313
Why don’t you tell us about them."

60
00:03:00.915 --> 00:03:04.678
Zann and the others followed the man into a surprisingly spacious cave.

61
00:03:05.619 --> 00:03:09.362
One nomad lit some candles while others brought out some food and drink.

62
00:03:10.182 --> 00:03:13.045
Zann and his friends told the nomads about Gliss and Wyssa.

63
00:03:13.765 --> 00:03:15.287
Half a dozen nomads stood up.

64
00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:18.890
They promised not to rest until they’d found the pair.

65
00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.611
"How will they find them?"

66
00:03:21.011 --> 00:03:23.093
Zann asked after the search party had left.

67
00:03:23.113 --> 00:03:26.256
"I thought it was hard to use magic here."

68
00:03:27.176 --> 00:03:29.197
"It is," the nomad leader said.

69
00:03:29.217 --> 00:03:34.741
"But we have learned to compensate for our home's unpredictable and weak magic."

70
00:03:35.622 --> 00:03:36.342
"What do you mean?"

71
00:03:36.622 --> 00:03:37.203
Darb asked.

72
00:03:38.123 --> 00:03:39.164
A woman stepped forward.

73
00:03:39.184 --> 00:03:43.527
"We know how to read the wind and the sound waves," she said.

74
00:03:43.547 --> 00:03:49.831
"And how to communicate with the creatures of the desert, who see and hear even more than we

75
00:03:49.871 --> 00:03:51.772
can." "Really?"

76
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:53.393
Darb looked impressed.

77
00:03:53.413 --> 00:03:56.956
"Wow." Zann was confused.

78
00:03:57.812 --> 00:04:03.157
He'd seen for himself that magic could be unpredictable here in the Far Frontier, just like it was

79
00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:04.398
near the Cave of the Unknown.

80
00:04:05.158 --> 00:04:07.300
But why had the nomad called it weak?

81
00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:11.604
If the Source was here, shouldn't magic be stronger than normal?

82
00:04:12.364 --> 00:04:16.968
He opened his mouth to ask the nomads about the Source, but Perda spoke before he could.

83
00:04:16.988 --> 00:04:21.892
"You said Morb was causing your tribe lots of trouble," she said.

84
00:04:21.912 --> 00:04:23.393
"What did he do?"

85
00:04:23.413 --> 00:04:28.069
"He's been using magic carelessly," the leader said with a frown.

86
00:04:28.089 --> 00:04:32.250
"He has no concern for how the stray energy affects others."

87
00:04:33.151 --> 00:04:34.351
Another nomad spoke up.

88
00:04:34.371 --> 00:04:41.014
"Yes, and he destroyed an ancient tree that was important to the history of a neighboring tribe."

89
00:04:41.034 --> 00:04:44.815
"Don't forget the Seeing Stone," a woman said.

90
00:04:45.636 --> 00:04:46.496
She looked at the kids.

91
00:04:47.817 --> 00:04:52.999
"Morb appears to be building something on a plateau that we use for seeing long distances."

92
00:04:54.219 --> 00:04:55.120
"What is he building?"

93
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.080
Zann asked.

94
00:04:57.152 --> 00:05:00.815
He thought about the terrible magical contraptions Morb had built before.

95
00:05:00.835 --> 00:05:03.957
"And why would he be building it way out here?"

96
00:05:04.377 --> 00:05:04.938
Darb added.

97
00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:10.321
"Maybe he's trying to build a device that will help him find the Source," Perda said.

98
00:05:10.341 --> 00:05:13.804
"Or to control it," Zann said.

99
00:05:13.824 --> 00:05:15.345
"The Source?"

100
00:05:15.965 --> 00:05:16.726
a nomad said.

101
00:05:16.746 --> 00:05:18.227
"What do you mean?"

102
00:05:18.247 --> 00:05:22.130
"The Source of all magic," Perda explained.

103
00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:28.789
"That's where the legends say all of Magica—" "We know what the Source of all magic is," a

104
00:05:28.829 --> 00:05:30.309
woman interrupted with a chuckle.

105
00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:36.031
"But if it actually exists, I can assure you it's nowhere in the Far Frontier!"

106
00:05:36.891 --> 00:05:39.932
Most of the other nomads were smiling or chuckling now too.

107
00:05:41.192 --> 00:05:41.973
Zann frowned.

108
00:05:41.993 --> 00:05:44.053
"How can you be so sure?"

109
00:05:44.073 --> 00:05:48.474
"There's no strong magic power here at all," the leader explained.

110
00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:52.395
"That's why this part of Magica was never heavily populated."

111
00:05:53.176 --> 00:05:54.376
Another nomad nodded.

112
00:05:55.104 --> 00:05:59.508
"We can barely muster enough magic energy to stay fed and clothed," she said.

113
00:05:59.528 --> 00:06:05.172
"We must rely on our own feet, and those of the hoof beasts, for transportation.

114
00:06:05.653 --> 00:06:08.015
We can't even create trees for shade!"

115
00:06:08.035 --> 00:06:10.597
"Trust us," the leader said.

116
00:06:10.617 --> 00:06:14.960
"We know better than anyone that there isn't a whole lot of magic nearby."

117
00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:18.743
Zann was pretty sure that the nomads were telling the truth.

118
00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:21.485
But he felt more perplexed than ever.

119
00:06:21.505 --> 00:06:25.821
"If Morb isn't looking for the Source, then what's he doing here?"

120
00:06:26.121 --> 00:06:26.481
he said.

121
00:06:27.242 --> 00:06:30.824
Before anyone could respond, a breathless nomad burst in.

122
00:06:30.844 --> 00:06:35.446
"I came as fast as I could," he exclaimed.

123
00:06:35.466 --> 00:06:37.868
"We think we've found your friend!"
